    <briefdescription>
<para>Gap-filler using piecewise linear interpolation. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>For a requested timestamp t located between two known observations at t0 and t1: value(t) = v0 + (v1 − v0) × (t − t0) / (t1 − t0)</para>
<para>Edge cases:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If t &lt; first known timestamp → forward-fill from the first point.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If t &gt; last known timestamp → backward-fill from the last point.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>When t0 == t1, v0 is returned directly. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
